From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: pas: add SM4450 ADSP and WPSS

ROCKNIX SM4450 series patch 0003, re-based onto stock Linux 7.1.2. Their
hunks sit on shikra (SM4650) PAS entries that stock does not have; the two
qcom_pas_data structs and the two of_match_id entries are unchanged, only the
surrounding context is taken from the real 7.1.2 file.

One deviation, ours: the ADSP descriptor's auto_boot is false, not true.
rproc_add() boots an auto_boot rproc from driver probe (remoteproc_core.c:2311),
and probe runs inside do_initcalls() (init/main.c:1490), which
kernel_init_freeable() reaches before run_init_process("/init") (init/main.c:1619)
- the request would be issued while the rootfs is still the unpacked ramdisk and
nothing under /vendor is mounted yet. The image it names is not in /vendor/firmware
either: 58 regular files sit directly under it in out/re/tree_vendor.tsv and the
only two .mdt on the whole partition are CAMERA_ICP.mdt and gen6_3_26_0_zap.mdt,
so adsp.mdt is not there at probe time or afterwards. It arrives with the two
fstab.default:55-56 lines that mount by-name/modem on /vendor/firmware_mnt and
by-name/dsp on /vendor/dsp, both plain late-fs `wait,slotselect` entries and both
behind the boot-device path first-stage never resolves; ueventd.rc:69 then names
/vendor/firmware_mnt/image/ as the directory the firmware loader should read. A
probe-time boot therefore cannot succeed, and it is not free of noise: it logs a
failed load on the one console we have on a first boot. It is at least not a
stall - rproc_trigger_auto_boot() uses request_firmware_nowait(FW_ACTION_UEVENT)
(remoteproc_core.c:1693), whose own comment says "so we can be built-in kernel
code, without hanging the boot process" - so the argument for false is that the
ROM already issues the one request that can succeed, from
init.qti.kernel.target.rc:10 at `on early-boot`, once late-fs has mounted the
images and ueventd is serving firmware_directories. That write goes to
/sys/kernel/boot_adsp/boot and lands in rproc_boot(), which is what the compat
driver is there to receive. Dropping the doomed attempt also loses nothing to
clean up: a failing rproc_boot() decrements the power ref it took (the
atomic_inc_return at :1930 unwound at :1954-1956), so the rproc is left exactly
as unbooted as it was.

WPSS keeps ROCKNIX's auto_boot = true. wpss.mdt is not on the vendor partition
either, so its probe-time request fails the same way - the difference is who
could boot it later. The ROM's only WPSS trigger is `write
/sys/kernel/icnss/wpss_boot 1` (init.vendor.wlan.rc:9, at `on early-boot`), and
that path belongs to icnss2.ko (vendor_dlkm /lib/modules/icnss2.ko, 460856
bytes, /vendor/lib/modules/ at runtime), which has no way to load under our
CONFIG_MODULES=n. Keeping the inherited value states the attempt rather than
quietly dropping it; Wi-Fi coming up is a separate question from booting.

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -1530,6 +1530,40 @@
 	.region_assign_vmid = QCOM_SCM_VMID_MSS_MSA,
 };
 
+static const struct qcom_pas_data sm4450_adsp_resource = {
+	.crash_reason_smem = 423,
+	.firmware_name = "adsp.mdt",
+	.pas_id = 1,
+	.minidump_id = 5,
+	.auto_boot = false,
+	.proxy_pd_names = (char*[]){
+		"lcx",
+		"lmx",
+		NULL
+	},
+	.load_state = "adsp",
+	.ssr_name = "lpass",
+	.sysmon_name = "adsp",
+	.ssctl_id = 0x14,
+};
+
+static const struct qcom_pas_data sm4450_wpss_resource = {
+	.crash_reason_smem = 626,
+	.firmware_name = "wpss.mdt",
+	.pas_id = 6,
+	.minidump_id = 4,
+	.auto_boot = true,
+	.proxy_pd_names = (char*[]){
+		"cx",
+		"mx",
+		NULL
+	},
+	.load_state = "wpss",
+	.ssr_name = "wpss",
+	.sysmon_name = "wpss",
+	.ssctl_id = 0x19,
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_pas_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-adsp-pas", .data = &sm8550_adsp_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,milos-adsp-pas", .data = &sm8550_adsp_resource },
@@ -1571,6 +1605,8 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-slpi-pas", .data = &sdm845_slpi_resource_init },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdx55-mpss-pas", .data = &sdx55_mpss_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdx75-mpss-pas", .data = &sm8650_mpss_resource },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm4450-adsp-pas", .data = &sm4450_adsp_resource },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm4450-wpss-pas", .data = &sm4450_wpss_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115-adsp-pas", .data = &adsp_resource_init },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115-cdsp-pas", .data = &cdsp_resource_init },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115-mpss-pas", .data = &sc8180x_mpss_resource },
